1
00:00:00,310 --> 00:00:03,670
Every cohort needs current investor and startup research.

2
00:00:03,990 --> 00:00:06,260
Keeping it up to date by hand is slow.

3
00:00:06,740 --> 00:00:10,170
With Startup Tarot, one operator keeps that research current,

4
00:00:10,310 --> 00:00:12,400
with Codex doing the careful groundwork.

5
00:00:12,930 --> 00:00:15,400
Founders get a ready-to-open copy of the app

6
00:00:15,400 --> 00:00:17,710
to choose their next small experiment.

7
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:19,510
People stay in charge.

8
00:00:19,960 --> 00:00:21,740
Every release needs human approval,

9
00:00:21,870 --> 00:00:24,380
and nothing is published or sent automatically.

10
00:00:24,980 --> 00:00:27,300
Private contact data stays out of releases,

11
00:00:27,300 --> 00:00:28,950
and every change is versioned,

12
00:00:28,950 --> 00:00:30,770
so earlier versions can be restored.

13
00:00:31,550 --> 00:00:34,620
We've demonstrated it with synthetic data on a local setup.

14
00:00:34,830 --> 00:00:37,190
It hasn't been tried with OpenFor's data yet.

15
00:00:37,750 --> 00:00:40,020
We're asking for one operator and a small,

16
00:00:40,150 --> 00:00:42,060
authorized dataset to run a pilot.
